EXPERIMENT 6: CASE STUDY OF FOOD DELIVERY APPLICATION – POSITIVE TEST SCENARIOS AND TEST CASES

## 1. AIM

To write a case study to identify and analyze the requirements of a Food Delivery Application and to prepare positive test scenarios and test cases for the application.

## 2. INTRODUCTION

A Food Delivery Application is an online platform that allows customers to order food from restaurants through the internet. Users can register, log in, search for restaurants, view food menus, add food items to the cart, make payments, and track their orders.

Positive testing is performed to verify whether the application works correctly when valid inputs and expected operations are provided.

## 3. REQUIREMENT ANALYSIS

### Functional Requirements

1. User Registration: New users should be able to create an account.
2. User Login: Registered users should be able to log in using valid credentials.
3. Restaurant Search: Users should be able to search for available restaurants.
4. Food Menu: Users should be able to view food items and their prices.
5. Add to Cart: Users should be able to add food items to the shopping cart.
6. Place Order: Users should be able to place food orders successfully.
7. Payment: Users should be able to complete payments using valid payment methods.
8. Order Tracking: Users should be able to track their food orders.
9. Order Confirmation: Users should receive order confirmation.
10. Logout: Users should be able to log out successfully.

### Non-Functional Requirements

1. The application should be user-friendly.
2. The application should respond quickly.
3. Customer information should be secure.
4. The application should support multiple users.
5. Payment transactions should be reliable.
6. Order tracking should provide updated information.
7. The application should work on different devices.

## 4. POSITIVE TEST SCENARIOS

Positive testing verifies whether the application works correctly with valid inputs.

| Scenario ID | Test Scenario |
|---|---|
| TS01 | Verify user registration with valid details. |
| TS02 | Verify login using valid username and password. |
| TS03 | Verify restaurant search using a valid location. |
| TS04 | Verify that restaurant details are displayed correctly. |
| TS05 | Verify that food menu items are displayed. |
| TS06 | Verify that food items can be added to the cart. |
| TS07 | Verify that the cart displays selected food items and prices. |
| TS08 | Verify that users can place orders successfully. |
| TS09 | Verify payment using valid payment details. |
| TS10 | Verify that order confirmation is displayed. |
| TS11 | Verify that users can track their food orders. |
| TS12 | Verify that users can log out successfully. |

## 5. POSITIVE TEST CASES

| Test Case ID | Test Steps | Test Data | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| TC01 | Open the application and enter valid registration details. Click Register. | Valid name, email and password | Account should be created successfully. |
| TC02 | Enter valid username and password. Click Login. | Registered username and password | User should log in successfully. |
| TC03 | Enter a valid location in the search section. | Chennai | Available restaurants should be displayed. |
| TC04 | Select a restaurant from the search results. | Available restaurant | Restaurant name and details should be displayed. |
| TC05 | Open the restaurant menu. | Selected restaurant | Available food items and prices should be displayed. |
| TC06 | Select a food item and click Add to Cart. | Pizza, Quantity: 1 | Food item should be added to the cart. |
| TC07 | Open the shopping cart. | Selected food items | Cart should display correct items, quantities and total price. |
| TC08 | Enter a valid delivery address and click Place Order. | Valid Chennai delivery address | Food order should be placed successfully. |
| TC09 | Select a payment method and enter valid payment details. | Valid payment information | Payment should be completed successfully. |
| TC10 | Complete the ordering process. | Valid order | Order confirmation and order ID should be displayed. |
| TC11 | Open the order tracking section. | Valid order ID | Current order status should be displayed. |
| TC12 | Click the Logout button. | Logged-in user | User should log out successfully. |

